{"type": "thinking", "text": "Keep-one ON, Sell Old Gear: Bronze Axe ×1 25, Iron Sword ×2 124, total 149. But wait — with keeper ON, items with qty 1 should be excluded (keep the last one). Bronze Axe has 2 in inventory, 1 equipped → 1 sellable, keeper reservation? If keep one of each in inventory, you'd keep the last spare; but one is equipped. Hmm, results: Bronze Axe still ×1 sellable, Iron Sword ×2 sellable (3 inv, 1 equipped, keeper would keep 1 more → sell 1?). \n\nCompare with toggle OFF: Bronze Axe ×1, Iron Sword ×2, same! So \"Keep one of each item\" had NO effect on Sell Old Gear here. Hmm, that seems wrong. With keeper ON, Sell Old Gear should exclude keeping? Wait, all items in the old gear list with qty 1 disappeared (Adamantite etc.) — with OFF there were 11 rows, now only 2 rows even though the list includes only Bronze Axe and Iron Sword. Hmm wait, all the platebodies had qty 1, so keeper ON excludes them (keep one). That makes sense. And Bronze Axe (2 inv, 1 equipped) sells 1, Iron Sword (3 inv, 1 equipped) sells 2.\n\nHmm, if keeper semantics = keep at least 1 in inventory, then for Iron Sword: inventory 3 includes equipped one? If equipped is included in the 3, then to keep 1 in inventory you can sell 2 (the equipped one is the one kept). That matches ×2. For Bronze Axe: 2 in inventory including equipped, keep 1 → sell 1. Matches. So keeper effect correctly excludes the qty-1 items. OK so no bug — but wait, in the earlier per-item panel with keeper ON, Iron Sword showed only 1 sellable (62), whereas bulk Sell Old Gear with keeper ON sells 2 Iron Swords (124). Inconsistency! Per-item panel with keeper ON computes 3 - 1 equipped - 1 keeper = 1; bulk computes 3 - 1 equipped = 2. Hmm, that's an inconsistency between per-item trade-in and bulk clearance. Which is right?\n\nThe changed note: \"Per-item trade-in panel: the reserved keeper quantity is now computed from the inventory alone, as a separate step.\" That hints the per-item reserved keeper computation may be wrong — computing from inventory alone, then subtracting equipped separately could double-count. Actually maybe the bug is that the per-item panel reserves a keeper even when one is equipped, which makes per-item sell quantity lower than bulk. Is that a bug worth reporting? It's an inconsistency: with \"Keep one of each item\" ON, bulk Sell Old Gear offers 2 Iron Swords while per-item panel offers 1 with no ability to choose 2. Hmm.\n\nBut wait, whether the per-item panel had a stepper hidden due to qty 1: yes. If it's intentionally 1, then the discrepancy is real. Let's verify per-item panel with keeper ON for Iron Sword again carefully, and also for Bronze Axe (2 inv, 1 equipped): expect 0 sellable if double-subtracting (would maybe hide from panel or show 0). If per-item shows 0 for Bronze Axe, that's clearly inconsistent with bulk (which sells 1). Let's check.\n\nFirst, exit this sheet (cancel), go to All items and open Bronze Axe. Need to find Bronze Axe in list; scroll. Let me cancel."}
