{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting: Bronze Axe per-item shows a toast/snackbar \"Bronze Axe is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" So equipped tools cannot be sold per-item. But bulk Sell Old Gear includes Bronze Axe ×1 to sell! That's inconsistent: bulk sells an equipped item (Bronze Axe) despite per-item requiring unequip first. Also Iron Sword equipped but per-item panel was allowed (showed quantity 2) — hmm, wait, Iron Sword per-item panel earlier allowed selling 2 with keep OFF even though Iron Sword is equipped. Let me check: Iron Sword \"(equipped)\" and per-item panel allowed 2. So maybe per-item protects only if inventory count == 1? Or maybe for Iron Sword, \"equipped\" is a separate copy, while Bronze Axe x2 means one equipped and... hmm.\n\nActually perhaps equipped Item is a flag on an item stack; the per-item check is \"if this item is equipped and quantity <= 1, block.\" Iron Sword quantity 3 >1 so allowed; sellable max = qty - equipped = 2. Bronze Axe qty 2... should be allowed then with max 1. But it blocked. Hmm, why?\n\nWait, maybe the toast appeared because after tapping Bronze Axe, the panel opening failed? Actually maybe the per-item sheet opened and got dismissed? We only see toast. Hmm.\n\nHmm, maybe the block is because Bronze Axe is a tool, and equipped tools are mandatory? No, the message says \"Unequip it first to sell.\"\n\nActually maybe the rule: if item is equipped and it's the same stack, block; Iron Sword per-item allowed because... hmm, contradictory.\n\nLet me re-check Iron Sword: maybe Iron Sword being equipped, but the panel appears with max 2 selling; hmm perhaps the equipped Iron Sword is a separate equipment slot and inventory has 3 spares? While Bronze Axe x2 includes the equipped one. Inconsistent data modeling, but from a UI standpoint it's inconsistent that the per-item panel allowed selling Iron Sword while equipped (max 2 = 3-1) but blocked Bronze Axe.\n\nHmm, but wait: maybe the block for Bronze Axe is due to keeper ON? No message clearly says equipped.\n\nPerhaps the actual design: per-item panel can sell stacks, but if the item is equipped and selling all would leave none... Iron Sword: 3 in inventory - 2 sold = 1 left, which is the equipped one. Bronze Axe: 2 in inventory - 1 sold = 1 left (the equipped one), which should be fine. Hmm.\n\nUnless the keeper logic: with keeper ON, reserved keeper from inventory alone = 1; for Bronze Axe, sellable = 2 - 1 (keeper) = 1, then equipped check subtracts? would be 0 → block with message? But message says unequip. Hmm, and Iron Sword: 3 - 1 keeper = 2, then ... -1 equipped = 1 (matches earlier keeper ON panel showing 62 = 1). So with keeper ON, Iron Sword sellable 1, Bronze Axe sellable 0 → blocked with unequip toast... but a \"you can't sell because keeper is on\" message would be expected.\n\nThis is getting deep. Let me turn keeper OFF and test Bronze Axe per-item to see whether it's still blocked. If blocked with keeper OFF too, then it's an equipped-tool rule. Earlier bulk Sell Old Gear with keeper OFF included Bronze Axe ×1, which would then conflict.\n\nActually wait: does bulk Sell Old Gear actually sell equipped Bronze Axe? It listed it. Whether it executes correctly is another matter. We could test by selling all and checking equipment. That's a destructive but informative test. But it would also sell all my platebodies: Adamantite, Gilded, Mithril, Runite x2, Slayer, Steel helmet, Iron Swords — huge data changes. Not ideal, but testing bulk sale requires actual sale. Hmm. We could instead use Sell Junk for actual execution (Cowhide etc.) to test bulk execution, and analyze Sell Old Gear preview only.\n\nBut the potential bug \"bulk sell includes equipped item that per-item refuses to sell\" is significant. Let's verify per-item Bronze Axe with keeper OFF."}
