{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now Home screen in landscape! It shows \"Welcome back, Aldric!\" stats, Town section with only the first row of icon buttons (Shop, Inn, Guild Hall) as unlabeled Views at y=856 — the rest of the town grid (Church, Builder's Workshop, etc.), Gloomharvest event, No Active Session, are all cut off. This is a serious landscape issue: Home is unusable beyond the first row.\n\nThe developer couldn't reproduce the Gear landscape issue, but Home shows the same. Maybe landscape is simply not supported in this build; but the app doesn't lock orientation, and content is clipped.\n\nHmm wait, element [9] at (442,856), [10] (1199,856), [11] (1957,856) — these are Shop/Inn/Guild Hall buttons with no text? In landscape, the cards render but labels missing. Serious.\n\nCould this entire behavior be because the app's UI is designed for portrait and the developer's test device has a different behavior (e.g., resizeable)? Still a real bug from the user's perspective.\n\nBut the developer's reply \"could not reproduce\" suggests the issue might be an artifact of the test harness (e.g., the app's window didn't resize/reflow correctly because the emulator rotation left the app in a weird state). Actually, on Android, rotating the device doesn't resize the app window if the activity handles config changes / uses a fixed orientation; the app may be re-laid-out. Here it did re-layout (widths changed).\n\nMaybe the truth: the app's screens are scrollable, but the touch handling in landscape is broken in the app (swipe gestures don't scroll) — that's still an app bug.\n\nLet me test the tool's landscape swipe on the Home screen: swipe up from Town header (1200,779) which is a clickable? It's \"Town\" header clickable (collapsible). Swipe might collapse. Use x=1200,y=650 (empty area) upward."}
