{"type": "thinking", "text": "No scroll. Home content below the first row is inaccessible in landscape. Even if swipes were broken by the tool, the elements aren't present at all (Shop/Inn/Guild Hall show as unlabeled), so the app is clipping content. Actually the cards [9][10][11] with no text might be the Shop/Inn/Guild Hall buttons but labels not rendered? Hmm, in portrait they had text \"Shop\" etc. The observation may omit text for some reason.\n\nRegardless, this is a real landscape problem. But the developer didn't reproduce the Gear one. Maybe I should refile with a broader and clearer report: \"Landscape: Home (and other screens) content is clipped and unreachable; swiping doesn't scroll.\" Include Home as the screen, with the specific missing Town rows. The Home screen is not in the sweep areas though; but it's a system-level device bug affecting gear too.\n\nHmm, but if the developer rejects again, I shouldn't insist. Let me gather one more decisive piece of evidence: use the screenshot in landscape Home to show the cutoff. Also, maybe try a different rotation method: rotate portrait→landscape again with the Home screen to see if the content reflows/crops similarly (yes, deterministic).\n\nWait — an important nuance: when I rotated, the app's window may be *cropped*, e.g., the app still thinks it's 1080x2400 but the screen is 2400x1080. Look at Home landscape: \"Welcome back,\" at x=165, \"Aldric!\" at 134, stats at 177... those match portrait x coordinates (165,134,177)! And Combat Level \"80\" at x=302 (portrait 302), Total Level at 536 (portrait 536)! But Coins at 2182 (portrait 862) — different. Hmm, mixed. Actually \"Combat Level 80\" at x 135/260 in portrait vs \"Combat Level\" x=177? Let me compare: portrait Home: Combat Level at 177, 80 at 302, Total Level at 536, 720 at 653, Coins 862, 2.5M 954. Landscape Home: Combat Level 177, 80 at 302, Total Level 1196, 720 at 1313, Coins 2182, 2.5M 2274. So the first two are in old positions but the rest moved right. That suggests the layout is partially reflowed but the left part remains at portrait positions... The stats row might be a Row with weights; weird.\n\nLook at \"Welcome back,\" at 165, \"Aldric!\" at 134 — same as portrait. The title at 169 same. The shop cards at x 442,1199,1957 (portrait 222,539,857). So the Town grid reflowed to 3 columns across the wider screen.\n\nThe Town card row at y=856 shows only one row. The next row would be at y~1010+, below the bottom nav (975). So the content is simply taller than the available window and there's no scrolling. The Home screen in portrait is scrollable? In portrait, all content (stat header, town grid, event, no session) fit within 2400? The Home screen in portrait showed everything up to \"No Active Session\" at 1806-1860, with bottom nav at 2169 — yes it fit. So Home was not scrollable by design; in landscape it overflows and there's no scroll → clipped.\n\nThus the app lacks landscape support entirely. That is a real bug (device rotation), but maybe out of scope for the \"areas\" (shop, gear, bestiary)? It affects gear (reported) and bestiary and shop too probably.\n\nGiven the developer rejected the Gear landscape report, maybe their policy is that landscape is unsupported. I'll not re-report the same issue; instead I can mention it as a note at sign-off? The sign-off tool takes notes. I can mention the landscape observation and that it wasn't reproduced by dev. Hmm.\n\nMore important: continue finding bugs in the listed areas.\n\nLet me rotate back to portrait and continue.\n\nActually, wait. There's a subtle possibility: the tool's `rotate` may rotate the *device* but the app may be flagged as non-resizable and Android shows it in a letterboxed window. On Android 12+, non-resizable apps in landscape show letterboxed with the app fixed in portrait orientation, not reflowed. But the screenshot shows reflow, so resizeable.\n\nOK, rotate back to portrait."}
