{"type": "thinking", "text": "Back to Home portrait, all fine.\n\nNow let me test the quest board briefly (changed: available quests refreshed from character state each time board opens). Areas aren't quests but the change note hints at a bug. It's cheap to check: open Quests, see available quests; maybe complete one (Mining I etc. completed; guild quests completed 3). There may be an issue where completed quests still show as available or the list doesn't refresh after completing a quest.\n\nWe don't want to complete quests (data change). But we can check that available quests exclude completed ones and that the board refreshes after a state change. Hmm, hard without changing state. But let's look.\n\nActually, focus. Let me review the three areas more methodically for bugs.\n\nShop:\n- Buy tab: items with prices; strikethrough original prices. Buy quantity dialog with total. Check buy quantity input/boundary (e.g., set 0, sell...). Not changed except bulk actions. \n- Sell tab: filters, search, sort, keeper toggle, bulk previews, per-item panel, recent bulk sales. Found per-item bug.\n- Potential bug: \"Keep one of each item\" applies to Sell Junk/old gear; but the per-item panel when keeper ON reserves an extra copy (bug filed).\n- Buy: when buying an item already in inventory, quantity; total cost = price × qty; check for rounding/discount. Let's test buying 60 Logs (max?) and total cost 60×7=420. Also test buy more than affordable? 2.5M coins, max likely computed. Could test Basic Staff (375) with quantity 60 → 22,500; fine.\n\nMaybe test the XP Boost special item: \"1.8M coins\" with original \"2.5M coins\" — discounted. Buying it would spend 1.8M and grant boost; irreversible. Skip purchase; check the dialog.\n\nGear:\n- Slot chooser sorting correct; equipment changes persist; stats update.\n- Potential issue: chooser lists already-equipped item with \"Equip\" and allows re-equip (no-op). Not a bug.\n- Gear: \"Equip Best Gear\" button — test? It would equip multiple items; could revert manually but tedious. Maybe test and then unequip all to restore. Hmm, the starting state has Head/Body/Legs/Cape/Ring/Necklace/Shield empty; Equip Best Gear would fill them with best available (Mithril/Adamantite/Slayer/Runite/Gilded, Steel/Mithril helms, Agility/Mercantile capes). Reverting = unequip each (7 slots). Doable. It would test the chooser ranking indirectly and stat updates. But the risk: \"Equip Best Gear\" might choose weird items (a real bug in ranking?). Worth testing! The changed feature is \"candidate items are now ranked by their unlock threshold, with title as the tiebreak\" — this likely affects \"Equip Best Gear\" too? Actually the chooser ranking affects which item appears first, not which is best. But \"Equip Best Gear\" should pick highest stats, not first in chooser. Hmm.\n\nWait, the change \"candidate items are now ranked by their unlock threshold, with title as the tiebreak\" could mean the slot chooser list order only. The \"best gear\" selection should be by stats. Let's test \"Equip Best Gear\" and verify it equips the strongest items by defense:\n- Head: Steel Full Helmet Def +16 vs Mithril Med Helmet Def +16 — tie. Which is better? Same Def. Maybe Steel has other stats? The chooser showed both Def +16; tie broken by... Equip Best Gear might pick Steel (threshold 20) or Mithril (30). Hmm.\n- Body: Gilded +95 is best.\n- Legs: none.\n- Boots: Bronze Boots +5 only.\n- Cape: Agility vs Mercantile both Def +5 with different bonuses (XP +10% vs Yield +10%). \"Best\" ambiguous.\n- Shield: none.\n\n\"Equip Best Gear\" would equip Gilded Platebody (best def), Steel/Mithril helm, cape etc. That changes 4 slots; can revert by unequipping each. It's a good test of the changed ranking if the chooser is sorted such that the \"best\" item is first? Hmm, if the equip-best logic picks the first candidate in the sorted list (ascending unlock threshold), it would equip the WORST item (Mithril Platebody, Steel helmet) — that would be a bug! Wait: the Gear screen slot chooser candidates are sorted by unlock threshold; if \"Equip Best Gear\" uses the same sorted list and picks the first/last, it might pick by threshold, not stats. But \"Equip Best Gear\" likely has its own stat-based selection. Unknown.\n\nThe change note could indicate that the slot chooser's first item is meant to be the \"best available\" ranked by threshold? Hmm, \"candidate items are now ranked by their unlock threshold\" — ascending threshold means lowest-level first. For a chooser, sorted ascending seems odd; you'd usually show best/highest first. But \"ranked by unlock threshold, with title as tiebreak\" might mean descending (higher unlock = stronger). Our observation showed ascending (20 before 30; 30,40,45,50,50,60). So the app shows ascending. Could the intended ranking be descending? The change note doesn't say direction. Hmm. If the developer intended \"ranked by unlock threshold\" probably ascending (unlock order). Fine.\n\nLet's test Equip Best Gear. But this changes 5 slots; doable to revert.\n\nActually before that, test the slot chooser for Head: equip Steel Full Helmet, then open chooser again; is Steel listed first/equipped? Then unequip. Eh.\n\nLet me test \"Equip Best Gear\" — it's a prominent feature in the gear area. I'll revert afterwards. First record current gear: Head None, Body None, Legs None, Boots Bronze Boots, Cape None, Ring None, Necklace None, Shield None. Weapon Iron Sword.\n\nGo Profile > Gear? We're on Home; easier: tap Combat tab → Gear (top tab). The Combat Gear screen is reachable via Combat > Gear. Tap Combat nav (element 26)."}
