{"type": "thinking", "text": "Bonuses screen shows:\n- SKILL BONUSES\n- Attack: Prestige +5%, +5% XP\n- Attack: Boosts combat stats, +9\n- Hitpoints: Prestige +5%, +5% XP\n- Hitpoints: Boosts combat stats, +4\n- Construction: 0.5% off building upgrade costs per level, -7%, Builder's Workshop\n- Infinite Tower: +7% XP, Tower\n- Infinite Tower: +12% coin drops, Tower\n- Infinite Tower: +150 HP, Tower\n\nMatches the preconditions: Attack and Hitpoints prestiged once, Precision I&II (+9 Attack), Vitality I (+4 HP), construction level? -7% (level 14? given Smithing 19... construction not mentioned), Tower bonuses +7% XP, +12% coin drops, +150 HP. Looks consistent.\n\nHmm, but no equipment bonuses listed here? \"SKILL BONUSES\" only. Fine.\n\nNow let's look for more issues in the bestiary. Potential bug: The bestiary \"0 / 100 encountered\" but lists ~100. The \"All\" filter initially showed V-Z items only (likely stale scroll). Hmm.\n\nLet me think about the changed features again and where bugs could be planted:\n1. Shop bulk clearance preview total computed by separate pass before confirmation. — We verified Sell Junk total 468 matches 78+354+36 and actual sale gave 468, and Sell Old Gear total 5416 matched line items (after scrolling). Also keeper ON totals correct. No bug found. But maybe there's a bug in the preview when items change between preview and confirmation? \"computed by a separate pass before the confirmation step\" — maybe the preview shows the total for all junk including something not actually sold (e.g., items that are locked/keeper). The precondition says no item locked, so no.\n\nMaybe test Sell Old Gear preview total vs actual sale? That would be destructive but verifies the \"separate pass\" total. Suppose the total is computed in a separate pass including an item that's not actually sold, the toast would say a different amount. For Sell Junk, both matched. For Sell Old Gear, the preview total 5416; if we confirm we get a toast \"Sold old gear for