\" I'd stick to those, but a quick quest board check is low cost. Let's do it after bestiary.\n\nNow, the bestiary: any bug? Let's test the \"Missing\" filter after 0 encountered: All vs Missing should be identical (all missing). Compare counts? The progress shows 0/100. So All should equal Missing. The lists looked similar but not obviously identical (initially All showed V-Z due to scroll position; Missing showed A...). Hmm.\n\nWait — this is interesting: When I first opened Bestiary (All), the list showed Vine Beast...Zombie. When I toggled Missing, it showed Abyssal Guardian...Barrow Wight. Then toggling All again showed Abyssal Guardian...Barrow Wight. So the initial All list was scrolled to the end. This suggests the initial scroll offset was at the bottom. Could be because the previous page (Profile Gear) had been scrolled? No, different composable. Or because the app's bestiary list is initialized with scrollToEnd? That would be a UX bug (opens at bottom). But since 0 encountered, maybe the \"All\" list is sorted with encountered/recent first? Hmm.\n\nLet me re-open Bestiary fresh (navigate away and back) and see the initial scroll position again. If it consistently opens at the bottom, it's a reproducible bug: Bestiary opens scrolled to the last entries instead of the top. But is that severe? Minor. Also it might have been caused by my earlier swipe on the Bestiary screen (the portrait swipe from progress bar scrolled the list). Wait, the initial Bestiary visit was BEFORE any swipe on it. Sequence: first time I opened Bestiary, it showed V-Z. Then I tapped Missing → A... So it wasn't caused by my swipe (which came later). Unless the app had remembered scroll from a previous session (the scenario data may include persisted scroll state from a previous app use — unlikely but possible).\n\nActually, maybe I caused it inadvertently: when I opened Bestiary, the tap at element 16 might have been interpreted also as a scroll? No.\n\nHmm, let me test: navigate Profile→Bestiary fresh now. Currently on Bonuses. Tap Bestiary. Observe top item."}
