{"type": "thinking", "text": "Keeper ON, Bronze Dagger qty 1 (not equipped): toast \"Keeping your last Bronze Dagger (Keep one of each item is on).\" Good UX — correct.\n\nSo the per-item panel logic works for non-equipped; only double-subtracts equipped. The confirmed bug stands.\n\nInteresting: for Bronze Axe (equipped, 2 in inventory), instead of saying both reasons, it says \"equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" The correct would be \"Keeping your last Bronze Axe...\" if keeper reservation works on total inventory (2-1=1 sellable though...). Hmm wait: with keeper ON, the keeper reserves 1, leaving 1 sellable for Bronze Axe (2-1). It should be sellable, but the equipped flag then zeroes it. So the bug is exactly double-subtract. Good.\n\nNow let me consider whether there are bugs in the Bestiary detail sheet for an encountered creature. All are unencountered (0/100). Can't encounter without combat. Hmm, we could start a combat session with a creature to encounter it? That would take time/change state. Not necessary.\n\nLet's check the \"Bosses\" tab progress discrepancy once more: it says \"0 / 100 encountered\" on the Bosses tab. I could count bosses by scrolling the boss list to the end: we saw 7 items (Brood Empress to Sol Invictus) — maybe more beyond. Let's check by scrolling the Bosses A-Z list to bottom in portrait. If there are exactly 7 bosses and the header says /100, that's suspicious but might be shared progress. I'd rather not report.\n\nActually, maybe I should test the Bestiary \"By Location\" grouping for a creature with multiple locations (Void Guardian appears under first location only; it has \"Abyssal Ruins, Arcane Ruins\" — should it appear under both? In the By Location list, it appeared under Abyssal Ruins only (first location) and not under Arcane Ruins. Could be a bug: multi-location creatures only listed under first location. Let's check: By Location list under \"Arcane Ruins\" header — does Void Guardian appear there? Earlier when I switched to By Location, the visible list showed headers \"Abyssal Ruins\" then \"Abyssal Throne\"; Arcane Ruins would be below. We need to scroll to see. Also \"Void Guardian\" has locations \"Abyssal Ruins, Arcane Ruins\". If it's grouped only under Abyssal Ruins, that could be acceptable design (primary location) or a bug.\n\nHmm, that's a plausible planted bug for bestiary (grouping by location). Let's investigate: switch to By Location, Bosses tab off (Enemies), and scroll to \"Arcane Ruins\" section to see whether Void Guardian is listed. Currently on Shop Sell. Let's navigate to Profile > Bestiary and do this. It's a legitimate area test.\n\nAlso there's \"Ancient Forest Ruins\", \"Spider Den\", \"The Hollowfen\", \"Undead Crypt\" — the initial list of creatures with locations. By Location should group each creature under each of its locations.\n\nLet me go. Tap Profile nav then Bestiary."}
