for Logs (max 29 with keeper ON, 30 with keeper OFF). With keeper OFF, tap Logs → max 30. Enter 31 → should clamp to 30. Then enter 0 → 1. We already tested on Iron Sword. Fine.\n\nLet me also verify the per-item quantity stepper's \"Max\"/\"+10\"/\"180\" presets disabled states make sense: for max 29, \"60\", \"180\", \"Max\" disabled, \"+10\" enabled (29→39 clamped?). Hmm: In Logs keeper ON (max 29) earlier: \"Increase\" disabled (already at max 29), \"+10\" disabled, \"+100\" disabled, \"1\" enabled, \"60/180/Max\" disabled, \"-10/-100\" enabled. That's consistent: at max, cannot increase. If we set 1, then \"+10\" should become enabled and set to 11? Let's test quickly maybe not needed.\n\nLet me now check the gear slot chooser more rigorously for the tiebreak: Body list at threshold 50: Runite Chainbody then Runite Platebody (alphabetical). Good. What about Head at threshold 16 def both Steel/Mithril? Their req levels differ (20 vs 30). Cape: Agility and Mercantile both no req shown (maybe req 1); alphabetical. Good.\n\nWhat about Legs/Ring/Necklace/Shield: no items in inventory, so chooser shows empty? Let's check a slot with no candidates: e.g., Legs. Tapping it might show an empty sheet or a \"No items\" message. A missing empty state could be a bug but minor. Let's test Legs quickly. This is in the gear area. We're in Bestiary; navigate to Combat tab > Gear. Hmm, several taps. Let's do it: tap Combat nav (320,2210), then Gear tab."}
