{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! Switching to Strength shows:\n- ATK 79  STR 70  DEF 191\n- Weapon (Str): None\n- Head: Steel Full Helmet Def +16 equipped\n- Body: Gilded Platebody Def +95 equipped\n- Cape: Agility Cape equipped\n\nWait, I unequipped Head/Body/Cape earlier! Yet now they show equipped. Did my \"Equip Best Gear\" changes not revert? Let me scroll back: After Equip Best Gear I unequipped Head (DEF 175), Body (DEF 80), Cape (DEF 75). Then I went to Profile... The Gear screen at that time showed DEF 75 with all None. Then later... hmm, now switching combat style to Strength shows them equipped again with DEF 191. That's alarming: the equipment state reverted to the \"Equip Best Gear\" result when switching combat style! Or maybe when switching style, the game auto-equipped best gear? No.\n\nWait, look at the sequence: after unequipping all and returning to Combat Gear (via Combat nav just now), the screen showed Head None, Body None, Cape None, DEF 75. Then I tapped Legs (empty chooser), closed, tapped Strength. Now Head=Steel, Body=Gilded, Cape=Agility, DEF 191. So the equipment got re-equipped when switching combat style from Attack to Strength! That is a bug! Or... maybe the COMBAT STYLE switch triggers different loadouts: maybe each combat style has its own gear loadout, and switching restores the Strength loadout? Hmm, that's plausible: per-style equipment sets? The precondition only has one set. If each style has separate loadouts, then switching to Strength shows the Strength loadout, which included the gear I equipped while on Attack? Hmm, but I equipped Best Gear while on Attack style. If loadouts are per-style, equipping while Attack wouldn't affect Strength. Yet Strength shows the equipped gear.\n\nAlternatively, the app's gear screen might have a bug: switching style re-loads equipment from a stale/saved snapshot. But wait — maybe the equip/unequip actions I performed after \"Equip Best Gear\" were on the *Attack* style screen, and the Strength style is a separate loadout that defaults to the \"best gear\" auto-equip? Hmm.\n\nActually, could it be that the \"Equip Best Gear\" and unequip operations applied to a shared set, and switching style triggered a re-sync from `character.equipment` while the unequip operations only updated the local UI? That would be a persistence bug: the unequips didn't persist. But earlier, after unequipping, I left the Gear screen and returned via Profile → View Combat Gear, and it still showed None/DEF 75. Actually wait, did I? Let me trace: After unequip actions, screen showed DEF 75 and Head/Body/Cape None. Then I tapped Profile nav (980,2210) → Profile (Bonuses tab later). I didn't return to Combat Gear in Attack style before switching. Hmm, I did go to Profile → Armory/Bonuses/Bestiary. Then Combat nav → Gear → it showed Head/Body/Cape None, DEF 75. So the unequip persisted across leaving and coming back (Attack style).\n\nThen switching to Strength shows the gear equipped again. So either:\n(a) Switching combat style re-equips a stale set (bug), or\n(b) Each style has its own loadout and Strength retained the \"best gear\" loadout... but how would Strength get it if it was equipped in Attack? Maybe the loadout is shared but the game auto-equips best items when switching style? That seems unlikely.\n\nAlso ATK changed from 89 to 79, STR from 79 to 70. That's consistent with the weapon being unequipped for Strength style: the Iron Sword (Atk) provides Atk +10 and Str +9 to the Attack-style display. When style is Strength, the weapon slot is \"Weapon (Str)\" (none), so ATK 79 = 70+9 prestige, STR 70 = base. Hmm, but earlier when Attack style with Iron Sword: ATK 89 (70+9+10), STR 79 (70+9). Now Strength: ATK 79, STR 70. So the base Attack bonus +9 applies to ATK; the sword's +10/+9 no longer counted because weapon slot is for Str. OK that's consistent with a single equipment set: the Iron Sword is an \"Atk\" weapon, so in Strength style it's not equipped in the Str weapon slot. The other gear (Head/Body/Cape/Boots) still applies – hence DEF 191.\n\nSo the gear (Head/Body/Cape) is definitely equipped again. Did the game auto-equip them when switching to Strength? The \"Equip Best Gear\" button might have been pressed again inadvertently? I tapped element 5 (Strength). Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe my earlier unequip actions didn't persist because the Combat Gear screen state I saw after unequipping was from a fresh load? No...\n\nLet me investigate: switch back to Attack style and see the gear state."}
