ear in Attack, it also updated the Strength loadout? Hmm, that doesn't make sense unless the loadout is shared but the UI caches.\n\nAlternatively, the equipment is shared, and each style tab's UI is not refreshed from the store when switching. The Attack tab's UI reflects the live store (updated by my unequips); the Strength tab's UI was rendered once (in step 3) and cached; switching back to it doesn't re-read the store. If the gear data is shared, the Strength tab showing what was there last time is a UI stale-state bug. But the DEF value also shows 191 vs 75 — the combat stats row is computed per style from... maybe cached too.\n\nWhich is the real behavior? We can test by performing a change in Strength style (e.g., unequip Head) and then switching to Attack and back. If changes in Strength affect Attack's equipment, then the store is shared and the UI is stale per tab. If they're independent, then per-style loadouts exist (weird for this app, but possible).\n\nTest: In Strength style, unequip Head (element 12's Unequip at 1007,890). Then switch Attack and see. Let's do it."}
