{"type": "thinking", "text": "Strength persisted Head None, Body Gilded, Cape Agility, DEF 175.\n\nSo the app has per-combat-style equipment loadouts (at least for display). But is that plausible? The weapon slot is style-specific (Weapon (Atk) vs Weapon (Str)), and armor might be shared across styles. If armor were shared, unequipping Head in Strength would also remove it in Attack — it didn't (Attack Head None anyway; inconclusive). Let's test shared vs separate with a slot: In Strength, Body Gilded is equipped; in Attack, Body None. So body armor differs by style → per-style loadouts. That's actually a plausible game design (equipment presets per combat style). Hmm, but is it documented? The Gear screen shows combat style tabs, suggesting each style has its own gear. So per-style loadout is likely intentional.\n\nThen how did the Strength loadout get the Best Gear items? Maybe pressing \"Equip Best Gear\" equipped best gear for ALL styles (or the app's state is global and the Attack tab's display is the one that's stale?). Wait, now Attack shows none, Strength shows Gilded. If global equipment were shared, both would show the same. They differ → separate. So Equip Best Gear populated the Strength loadout as well? That's odd.\n\nAlternative explanation: The app stores one equipment set per combat style; the \"Equip Best Gear\" button actions might apply to the currently selected style (Attack) only... then Strength shouldn't have them.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the app's underlying model has a single equipment map but the UI stores remember per-tab state, and updates aren't propagated. The DEF value differs per tab (75 vs 175), which would be computed from the shared equipment? If shared, both should show same DEF. So the stats also cached per tab. So the app caches the entire screen state per style. But then the equipment state (shared) might be one of the two, and the display is stale.\n\nWhich state is real? Check an external view: the Profile > Gear tab (gathering tools) doesn't show combat gear. The Profile > Armory shows obtained items but not equipped. The Combat Dungeons screen might show a summary? The Home stats? Hmm. The \"ATK/STR/DEF\" shown per style likely derives from the actual combat loadout used for that style. If separate loadouts exist, then there are up to 4 sets of armor, each with its own state. But the inventory has only ONE Gilded Platebody. It can't be equipped in both Attack (if it were) and Strength simultaneously. Currently only Strength has it. OK.\n\nSo the \"Equip Best Gear\" performed on Attack style may have equipped gear for all styles? Or maybe I misremember which style was selected when I hit Equip Best Gear. Let me check: earlier, before pressing Equip Best Gear, the screen observation showed Attack [checked]. Yes. After pressing, Attack showed the gear. Then I unequipped in Attack. Now Strength shows the same gear minus Head (which I unequipped while in Strength). So Strength's loadout exactly mirrors the post-Equip-Best-Gear state. This strongly suggests the equipment WAS shared/global at Equip Best Gear time, and the Attack tab's unequip actions were applied to a per-tab copy... \n\nUgh. Let me look at how the app behaves with a definitive test: equip a specific item in Attack (e.g., Steel Full Helmet) and then check Strength. If Strength's Head shows Steel too, then the loadouts are shared and the UI caching is the issue (the unequip display in Attack would be wrong/stale). If Strength's Head stays None, then per-style loadouts.\n\nCurrently Strength: Head None, Body Gilded, Cape Agility, Boots, DEF 175.\nAttack: all None except Boots, DEF 75.\n\nTest: In Attack, equip Steel Full Helmet (via Head chooser). Then switch to Strength and check Head. But then I'd need to revert both styles.\n\nActually, simpler: The discrepancy itself is a bug regardless of design: the same character's gear screen shows different equipped Body item depending on the selected combat style, while there is only one Mithril/Gilded Platebody in inventory. If the game intends per-style loadouts, then the inventory item is \"equipped\" in two styles? In Attack Body None so only one. Fine. But then the item allocation is plausible.\n\nHmm, but the key question: is the equipment state per style, and did \"Equip Best Gear\" apply to all styles? Let's test with another change: In Strength, unequip Body (Gilded). Then switch to Attack — Body already None. Switch back — Body None. No help.\n\nBetter: In Strength, equip the Gilded Body? It's already. In Attack, open Body chooser; does it list Gilded Platebody as available? If Gilded is equipped in Strength, and loadouts are per-style, the item should still be available for Attack (or maybe not, if it's \"in use\" by another style). Equipping it in Attack would reveal shared vs separate.\n\nThis is a potential big bug: equipment not shared/consistent across styles. But it might be an intended design (combat loadouts per style). Most idle games have per-style loadouts? Some do.\n\nActually, the presence of \"COMBAT STYLE\" tabs on the Gear screen (Attack/Strength/Ranged/Magic) with the gear changing per style strongly implies per-style loadouts. The default \"Attack\" gear has Iron Sword; Strength shows no weapon. Each style has its own gear set. So the app is designed with loadouts per style. Then \"Equip Best Gear\" likely equips best for the selected style only. So why does Strength have Gilded/Body and Agility/Cape? Because when I pressed \"Equip Best Gear\" the selected style... maybe actually Strength was selected? No, the observation at that time showed Attack checked.\n\nWait, let me look back: The Equip Best Gear step: I was on Combat Gear with Attack checked. I tapped element 21 \"Equip Best Gear\". The result observation showed Attack checked with Head Steel, Body Gilded, Cape Agility. Then I unequipped Head, Body, Cape. Then I went to Profile → Armory → Bonuses → Bestiary → Quests → ... → Combat → Gear. The observation showed Attack checked with None. So far, consistent.\n\nThen I tapped Legs chooser (Attack, empty), closed, then tapped Strength. Strength showed the gear equipped. \n\nCould it be that when I tapped Strength, the app loaded the *saved loadout for Strength* which was default from some earlier state? At the start, all loadouts were probably empty except Boots/Iron Sword (weapon). Hmm, but Strength's Body Gilded and Cape Agility were never equipped by me in Strength.\n\nUnless \"Equip Best Gear\" equipped best gear for ALL combat styles at once. That's plausible: the button might gear up all styles. In that case, both Attack and Strength got Gilded etc. Then my unequips in Attack removed from Attack only. That is consistent! And \"per-style loadouts\" is the design.\n\nSo per-style loadouts exist and Equip Best Gear applies to all styles. Then no bug. But then the same single Gilded Platebody is equipped in both Attack and Strength loadouts simultaneously — item duplication across loadouts. Is that a bug? In many games with loadout presets, a single item can be referenced by multiple presets (only one active at a time). Since only one style is active for combat, it's fine.\n\nHmm, but if the inventory has only one Gilded Platebody, having it equipped in 4 loadouts means when you switch styles you're wearing it. That's acceptable design (loadout presets, not physical allocation).\n\nBut wait: I unequipped Body in Attack, yet Strength still had it. If loadouts are independent, that's fine.\n\nI should check whether switching styles in the app is even persisted/affects the game. Not relevant.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I won't report the loadout thing. But I need to restore the data: the Strength loadout now has Head None, Body Gilded, Cape Agility; Attack has none. To restore the starting state, I should unequip Body and Cape in Strength, then check all four styles are clean except Boots. But were the other styles (Ranged/Magic) also given gear by Equip Best Gear? Let me check