{"type": "thinking", "text": "Ranged style also has Head Steel, Body Gilded, Cape Agility, DEF 191. So \"Equip Best Gear\" equipped all four styles. This confirms per-style loadouts and Equip Best Gear applies to all (or the gear is shared across styles and per-tab caching).\n\nWait, the Head is Steel here but in Strength I unequipped Head. So Ranged still has Steel. Attack has None (I unequipped). Strength None. So per-style independent.\n\nNow Magic too likely. So the starting state per precondition only had Boots equipped (and Iron Sword). Equip Best Gear has equipped 3 items per style × 4 styles. I need to revert all styles: unequip Head/Body/Cape in Strength, Ranged, Magic (Attack already done). That's 9 more unequips. To restore to preconditions (equipped: Iron Sword, Bronze Pickaxe, Bronze Axe, Bronze Fishing Rod, Bronze Boots), I should clear all four styles' Head/Body/Cape. Wait, but were the other styles' equipment empty at start? The precondition says equipped only those items, implying all styles' armor empty except Boots (Boots may be shared or per style? It shows Bronze Boots in each style).\n\nHmm, was the starting state per-style all empty? We only saw Attack at first. The other styles might have had gear equipped from the start (the scenario data could have per-style loadouts). If so, my Equip Best Gear changed them, and I can't restore their original state exactly. Ugh. But if the underlying model is a single equipment set, then the per-style displays are copies of the same set, and equipping in any style affects all. Then my unequips in Attack should have changed all — but Ranged/Strength still show the gear, so no.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the truth is the opposite: there is ONE equipment set, and the UI caches a snapshot per style tab when first rendered. When I hit Equip Best Gear in Attack, all style tabs had not been rendered yet (except Attack). Then switching to Strength/Ranged renders them for the first time reading the then-current equipment set (Gilded etc. at that time), while Attack's tab re-reads live. But I unequipped the gear in Attack before rendering Strength/Ranged; if they read the live set, they'd show None. They showed Gilded. So they're not reading live. Unless the unequips only modified a per-style copy.\n\nAlternatively, the per-style UI states are stored in memory and initialized from the global set once (when the screen was first composed for each style). Hmm, but Strength was never composed before.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the tabs are all composed simultaneously (all four screens in a pager) when the Gear screen loads. So when I first opened the Gear screen (at the very start), all four style screens composed and cached the then-current equipment: all None except Boots/Iron Sword. Hmm, then after Equip Best Gear in Attack, the other tabs would still have cached None (not Gilded). But they showed Gilded. So no.\n\nCould the \"Equip Best Gear\" button have equipped gear for all styles (calling the same store with style parameter for each)? Then the state per style is: Attack/Strength/Ranged/Magic all Gilded etc. Then my unequips in Attack and Strength removed only those styles' copies. That fits perfectly: per-style loadouts, and Equip Best Gear equips best for all styles at once. Fine, no bug.\n\nNow I need to restore: unequip Head/Body/Cape in Strength, Ranged, Magic. Attack already clean. Also check whether Equip Best Gear modified the Iron Sword/weapon for other styles? Weapon (Ranged) None, Weapon (Str) None, so no. Good.\n\nI'll do the unequips in Ranged now: Head (14), Body (16), Cape (21). Careful indices shift after each. Let's do Head first."}
