{"type": "thinking", "text": "All four styles restored to only Bronze Boots (DEF 75). Attack style also verified earlier. Good.\n\nNow, the per-style loadout observation is interesting but likely intended. Is there a real consistency bug: the same item (Gilded Platebody) can be equipped in multiple styles at once even though there's only one copy? If per-style loadouts are intended, that's fine (loadout presets). But if equipment is supposed to be a single set, then this is an item duplication bug. The UI makes it clear that each style has its own equipment — the \"Weapon (Atk)\" vs \"Weapon (Str)\" slots differ. So per-style loadouts are a feature. No report.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually, maybe the per-style gear is intended to be separate but the INVENTORY item count should decrease when equipped? In the inventory, does equipping remove the item from inventory? The precondition inventory still lists equipped items (Iron Sword x3 with one equipped). So equipment is tracked as a flag within inventory, not subtracted. With per-style loadouts, the same Gilded Platebody could be flagged equipped in multiple styles. That's plausible if equipping doesn't consume the item but marks it equipped for a style. Fine.\n\nLet me now revisit the shop's \"Keep one of each item\" persistence and set it back to OFF. Currently it's ON (we turned it ON last). Let me set it OFF to restore precondition.\n\nAlso, I should verify the coin count didn't change unexpectedly? We bought/sold: sold 1 log +6, sold junk +468, bought 1 log -7 → net +467 from 2,567,890 = 2,568,357. Display 2.5M. Can't verify exact. Fine.\n\nBut wait, we sold 13 Cowhide/59 Feather/6 Wool, which can't be restored. Data changed, but it was necessary to test bulk. Similarly inventory Logs restored to 30. Fine.\n\nNow, set keeper OFF. Go Shop → Sell."}
