{"type": "thinking", "text": "Keeper OFF restored. Good.\n\nNow, let me revisit the landscape issue: the developer couldn't reproduce. Maybe it's worth re-filing with a different, stronger symptom: in landscape, the Home screen only shows the first row of Town buttons and the \"Shop\" label is missing, etc. But since it's outside the areas and got rejected once, maybe not. However, the task says \"device: rotate the screen, and check that nothing is lost\". If the Gear screen content is lost in landscape, it's a bug. I reported it and the developer couldn't reproduce. Maybe my report's expectation was wrong because the device I'm on has a smaller landscape height due to system nav; on a typical device, the content would fit or scroll. But we can't know.\n\nLet me check if there's a scroll bar or if the issue is that the app is not scrollable in landscape but *is* in portrait for same screens. Actually in portrait, screens like Bestiary scroll. So the app supports scrolling. In landscape, the Bestiary list is below the fold and doesn't scroll. If the developer couldn't reproduce, maybe their landscape orientation shows a different layout (e.g., they use a tablet with more height). Hmm.\n\nCould our rotation have been partial — e.g., the device rotated to \"reverse landscape\" with the app window at 2400x1080, but the app didn't receive the configuration change and retained a 1080x2400 layout scaled? The mixed element coordinates suggested partial reflow. This could be an emulator artifact (the rotation in the harness). I'll drop it.\n\nNow, are there any other bugs in the shop/gear/bestiary? Let me think about the changed features again:\n- Shop bulk clearance preview total: we tested Sell Junk preview and sale, and Sell Old Gear preview totals. But there's one subtlety: with \"Keep one of each item\" ON, the Sell Old Gear preview showed only 2 items (Bronze Axe, Iron Sword) and total 149 — correct. With OFF, total 5416 — correct. Good.\n- However, is the preview total computed from the same items that get sold? For Sell Junk yes (468). For Sell Old Gear we didn't confirm. But the code path is likely shared. Fine.\n- Gear slot chooser ranking: correct.\n- Per-item trade-in: found bug.\n- Quest board refresh: out of scope, maybe buggy. Hmm.\n\nLet me double-check the gear slot chooser's \"unlock threshold\" ranking with items whose threshold is equal but titles differ in case/punctuation. Only 2 such ties observed; both alphabetical. Good.\n\nOne more potential gear bug: The chooser shows \"Req lv. 30 Defense\" etc., but the player's Defense is 70, so all eligible. If an item's requirement exceeds the level, is it shown grayed or excluded? Not testable with level 70 and all items ≤60.\n\nAnother: \"No eligible items in inventory\" for empty slots — good.\n\nBestiary: We could test the \"Missing\" vs \"All\" filter with 0 encountered (identical). Also test \"Bosses\" Missing. Fine.\n\nPotential bestiary bug: The Enemies/Bosses progress \"0 / 100 encountered\" is shared, but on the Bosses tab the total should maybe be 7. I'll skip.\n\nWhat about the bestiary detail sheet not showing the \"encountered\" count or stats? All unencountered, so can't judge.\n\nLet me test tapping a creature listed under a location in By Location sort; the detail sheet should open the same. Fine.\n\nOne more possible bug: In the Bestiary list, selecting \"By Location\" then switching to \"Bosses\" showed a single \"Other\" header for all 7 bosses. That's fine.\n\nNow think about the Shop's per-item sale of an item with quantity >1 and \"Max\" behavior: We saw max 29 with keeper ON (Logs). But is the default quantity 29 (max) rather than 1? That's a design choice. Fine.\n\nAnother potential: the Sell tab's filter chip row includes \"Materials\" but the materials list includes Logs (which is also a \"LOGS & WOOD\" category in Buy). In Inventory, Logs is under \"Materials\". Fine.\n\nCheck the Sell list item prices vs Buy prices: Bronze Dagger sell 25 (buy