uest\" — Mining I is completed, so Mining II should be available. Unless Mining II requires Mining level 60 (Mining 50). Similarly Fishing II requires Fishing level 40 (Fishing 30), Woodcutting II requires Woodcutting 40 (WC 30). And Thieving I requires Thieving level? Thieving is 1, and the quest \"Pickpocket 100 Peasants\" might require Thieving 10. So all the gray quests could be level-locked. That's consistent! The white Crafting I quests might have low/no level requirements (Smithing I completed at 19, Cooking 25...). Hmm, but Cooking—Fish I white with Cooking 25; Cooking—Beef I white (Cooking 25). So maybe those have no req.\n\nOK, no bug.\n\nLet me consider testing the \"Recent bulk sales\" persistence: the entry was shown \"0 minutes ago\". If we leave and return, does it persist? Probably. Let's check: tap Shop Sell → Recent bulk sales. It may show the record. We already did that. Fine.\n\nOne more shop edge: buying the 2× XP Boost when one was purchased this week should block. Not testable without buying (1.8M). Skip.\n\nLet me check the \"Sell Old Gear\" preview total after our changes with keeper OFF to confirm it's stable and matches line items: 5416. Quick check: tap Sell Old Gear."}
