{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now, before signing off, let me reconsider the landscape bug and whether to report it again with Home as the screen. The developer couldn't reproduce the Gear one. I shouldn't spam. But maybe I can craft a better report: the device rotation leaves the app at a landscape layout where scroll doesn't work. Hmm, but our swipe tool seems unreliable, and the developer's test presumably uses the same kind of automation? They said \"could not reproduce with the steps given\" — maybe the UI is actually scrollable on their device and our observation missed it because the list's scroll is implemented with a gesture that our tool fails to trigger in landscape. I'll leave it, and mention in sign-off notes.\n\nBut wait — I should double check the landscape issue isn't due to the app's \"portrait\" orientation being rotated via a config the app ignores, i.e., the app may be non-resizable and Android applies a fixed-size compat mode. On many devices, apps that don't support landscape get a rotated letterboxed portrait UI. Here the UI clearly reflowed (3 columns in Town), so it supports landscape. And the content got cut with no scroll. This is likely a genuine bug. But the developer says no. Maybe because they tested from a different starting point (e.g., their screen scrolled?). I could file again with the Home screen to show it's not limited to Gear. But duplicate-ish. The instructions: \"Reproduce a problem once before you report it.\" I reproduced multiple times. The developer reply isn't necessarily final; I can file another report for a different screen. But if they can't reproduce, it won't be logged, and I've spent effort.\n\nHmm. Maybe the \"could not reproduce\" is because the expected behavior I described was wrong: they might consider it fine that content requires scrolling, and on their device the scroll works. If the list is scrollable in landscape on a real device, then our tool's swipe failure is a harness limitation. So a re-report would be noise. I'll skip.\n\nLet me do a final check of the per-item sale panel against the changed note in one more scenario to ensure my report is accurate: with keeper ON, per-item Iron Sword should show 1 (observed), and with keeper OFF show 2. Both observed. Good.\n\nWait, there's something else: with keeper ON, per-item Logs shows 29 (correct), so the keeper reservation logic is fine for non-equipped. The bug is only for equipped. Since the change says \"computed from the inventory alone\", maybe the intended reserve is computed as min(1, inventory) then subtracted *along with* equipped. Our report says it double-subtracts. The developer confirmed and logged. Good.\n\nNow, is there a second bug in the same changed feature: with keeper ON, per-item Bronze Axe shows the wrong message \"Bronze Axe is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" instead of a keeper message. This is part of the same root cause; no separate report needed.\n\nLet me also check the case \"keeper OFF, per-item Iron Sword\" again — we saw 2 (124). Good.\n\nNow, the buy flow's quantity boundary: we tested type 99 → clamped to max; type 0 → 1. Fine.\n\nWhat about entering a non-numeric input in the quantity field? type_text \"abc\" — since it's a numeric keyboard, might not allow. Could test but not necessary.\n\nWhat about entering a very large number like 999999999 → clamped. Fine.\n\nLet me test one more potential bug in the per-item panel: the \"You'll receive\" total should update when you change quantity via the EditText BEFORE committing (i.e., live). When I typed 99, the preview stayed 124 (clamped to max 2). That's consistent with clamping. When I typed \"0\", it immediately clamped to 1 and preview 62. Fine. What if I type \"3\" when max 2? It might clamp to 2 live or on Enter. We saw 99 → preview 124 while field showed 99; then Enter clamped to 2. If the user taps Sell while the field shows 99, does it sell 2? The preview says 124, likely. Not a bug.\n\nWhat about the \"-100\"/\"-10\" buttons when quantity is 1 — disabled. Good.\n\nOK. Let me also quickly verify that the \"Recent bulk sales\" entry persists after leaving/returning and shows the correct details (it's a shop feature). Tap it now."}
