{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha: Under \"All\", searching \"Stone\" shows a \"MISC\" section with Stone ×12, 5 coins ea. So Stone is sellable but categorized as MISC, and there's no \"Misc\" filter chip — only All/Weapons/Armor/Tools/Materials. Therefore, when you filter by any category chip, Stone is not reachable via the filter; you can only find it via \"All\" or search. Is that a bug? The category chips might intentionally exclude misc items (they're not in the categories). The \"Materials\" chip omits Stone because Stone is \"Misc\". This is a UX gap but likely intended category design. Similarly Cowhide/Feather/Wool are probably MISC. Hmm, Cowhide is under \"Other\" in inventory but likely MISC in shop. Fine.\n\nNot a bug worth reporting.\n\nNow, there's a possibility the \"Sell Junk\" only includes certain junk items (Cowhide/Feather/Wool) and not Stone (Misc). Fine.\n\nI should reset the search (navigate away/back) to leave clean state. Let me tap back arrow (element 20) twice (first may just hide focus), then re-enter? Actually leaving the shop resets the Sell tab search? Earlier re-entering showed \"Search items\" placeholder. Yes. Let's leave the shop to Home (tap back arrow element 20 twice) and finish.\n\nActually one more thought: we could test the per-item sale of Stone with search; not needed.\n\nLet me now decide whether to report the landscape issue with Home. I'll skip reporting; mention in sign-off notes.\n\nBut wait, I should reconsider: the developer \"could not reproduce\" the landscape bug. It's possible the bug is real but only on this specific device/emulator (e.g., the system nav bar overlapping). Since the harness says \"operate a real Android device\" — it's a real device. The developer may have tested on a different device. The report was not confirmed, so it's not logged. To be diligent, I could file a second, more general report (Home screen landscape content inaccessible) so they have another data point. But it might be rejected as well. The instructions: \"When you find a bug, file a report. A developer will reply. A confirmed report is logged.\" It doesn't say we can't file unconfirmed ones. The risk is being seen as noisy. Hmm, the \"could not reproduce\" reply suggests my steps weren't enough. Maybe the developer's device auto-rotates back or the app locks orientation on their device (their emulator has rotation disabled), so they literally can't reproduce. In that case, a second report won't help.\n\nI'll mention it in the sign-off notes with the confidence.\n\nActually, let me try once more with a different approach to prove the app is at fault: In landscape on the Home screen, can I interact with the missing content via accessibility/element indices? The observation doesn't list them, so they're not in the accessibility tree — they may be truly not composed or clipped. If the list were scrollable, the off-screen items would still typically be in the tree? In Compose LazyColumn, off-screen items are not in the semantics tree. So not conclusive.\n\nGiven the developer's reply, I'll leave it.\n\nLet me now also double check the per-item bug report was reasonable; it was confirmed.\n\nBefore sign-off, restore the shop search (leave/re-enter or clear). Let me leave Shop to Home. Tap back arrow element 20, then again. Then maybe verify no other obvious state issue."}
