{"type": "thinking", "text": "Home, clean. Search reset when re-entering shop? We left; next entry resets. Fine.\n\nNow, before signing off, let me think if I should test the \"Quest board refresh\" change since it's listed. The sweep areas don't include it, but a quick test of the board opening might reveal an obvious bug like stale data. We saw the board shows completed quests correctly and daily quests. The \"available quests refreshed\" change might mean that when a quest becomes available (e.g., after a level up), opening the board updates it. Hard to test without a level change. We could use skills to change XP? Starting a session changes state and requires time. Skip.\n\nLet me think about the possibility that the bestiary has a bug I overlooked: the \"0 / 100 encountered\" counter vs the number of creatures in the list. If the enemies list truly has 93 entries, the counter 100 includes bosses. The Bosses tab shows the same counter — maybe intended global. Fine.\n\nAnother: The bestiary \"All\" filter at 0 encountered shows all creatures, and \"Missing\" also shows all. Fine.\n\nThe \"Bosses\" tab's \"0 / 100 encountered\" label says \"encountered\" while the boss list has 7 — not obviously wrong.\n\nOne more: In the Bestiary \"By Location\" view, the first partial row \"The Hollowfen\" appeared after scrolling; that could be a normal partially visible row from a section, showing only the location line because the creature name was scrolled above. Fine.\n\nOK. Now the shop \"Sell Old Gear\" item list includes Bronze Axe (a tool) — the panel is titled \"Sell Old Gear\" and includes tools. Is that expected? The bulk \"Sell Old Gear\" seems to include weapons, armor, AND tools (Bronze Axe). The category filters include Tools separately. Hmm, \"Sell Old Gear\" selling a Bronze Axe (a gathering tool) may be intentional (all equipment). Not a bug.\n\nBut notice: \"Sell Old Gear\" preview with keeper OFF includes Bronze Axe ×1 (a tool that is equipped? one of the 2). With keeper ON it still includes Bronze Axe ×1. Fine.\n\nWhat about Bronze Pickaxe x1 (equipped) and Bronze Fishing Rod x1 (equipped)? They're not in the old gear list (skills=1, tools maybe excluded). The Bronze Axe is in the list because qty 2 (one spare). Fine.\n\nAlright, I've done enough. But the task says \"exercise every one of them before you sign off\" and \"go past the happy path\" for each feature: state, reversal, repetition, input, consistency, device, navigation. I did most for shop and gear. For bestiary, I did filters/sorts/tabs/details, but not state/reversal (no mutable state except filters). Fine.\n\nActually, one more bestiary thing: the \"Missing\" filter should be the complement of encountered; with 0 encountered, All == Missing. The list count 100/100. Fine.\n\nI should also verify the bestiary detail sheet closes properly and doesn't lose the filters (state). We tapped a creature, closed, and the filter state (By Location etc.) persisted? After opening a boss detail and closing, the tab state remained. Fine.\n\nLet me consider whether to file a report about the Quest board's grayed-out available quests. The precondition says \"Quests completed: Mining I, Fishing I, Woodcutting I and Smithing I, plus 3 guild quests.\" On the Gathering tab, the II-tier quests appear grayed out — likely because they require higher levels. But the change note says available quests refresh from character state; maybe the II quests should be available now (Mining 50, Fishing 30, WC 30) and the gray state is a bug. Without knowing the requirements, risky. Skip.\n\nWait, the Crafting Skills tab shows all quests white, including \"Smithing I\" (completed, should maybe show Completed) — but Smithing I may be below the fold. Hmm, Smithing I is completed but I didn't see it; the list order was Construction I, Cooking—Fish I, Cooking—Beef I, Cooking—Chicken I, Cooking—Mutton I, Crafting I, Firemaking I, Fletching I, Herblore I, Prayer I, then (below) Smithing I, Smithing II... wait, alphabetically \"Smithing\" comes after \"Prayer\", yes. So it's below. It likely shows Completed + Reset. Fine.\n\nI'm fairly confident the three areas are covered.\n\nFinal decision on landscape: I'll include it in the sign-off notes as an observation that the dev couldn't reproduce, but not treat it as an open bug? The sign-off means \"you believe the listed areas have no remaining bugs\". If I believe the landscape issue is a real bug, I shouldn't sign off. Hmm. But the developer couldn't reproduce it; maybe it's a test-harness artifact. Given the evidence (multiple screens clipped, no scroll), I lean toward it being real on this device. But my report was rejected — maybe because the expected behavior was wrong? Let me re-read the reply: \"Developer: could not reproduce with the steps given.\" That's a non-confirmation. The developer didn't say \"by design\". Maybe I can try to reproduce once more with a slightly different route and then refile with the Home screen, giving exact steps and screenshot evidence. The system says \"A confirmed report is logged; no new build is installed.\" Unconfirmed reports aren't logged; that's fine, but I can still report.\n\nThe key question: is the app's landscape behavior a bug in the app or the harness? Let me test one more thing: whether the landscape screen scrolls when using a swipe that starts on a definitely non-interactive area and moves a long distance with a slower gesture. The tool only exposes direction/distance; maybe use distance 0.9. Earlier at x=686,y=1100 (progress bar) in Bestiary landscape, distance 0.5 did nothing. Try distance 0.9 from y=900 to y=90. Hmm.\n\nActually, I realize the likely cause: The app's root content is a `Column` with `verticalScroll` and the bottom nav is a separate bottom bar. In landscape, the content height is ~975; the Bestiary list is a `LazyColumn` with a fixed height (not weighted) or nested inside the scroll. If the outer Column doesn't scroll and the inner LazyColumn has no bounded height, it clips. The screens that scroll in portrait (Bestiary) use a LazyColumn with a fixed height fraction of the screen (e.g., 1700px in portrait) that in landscape becomes larger than the available space, so it overflows under the nav. The LazyColumn itself should still scroll when touched though, unless it's not receiving touch because the nav overlays. Hmm, the visible part of the list (0 px in landscape) isn't rendered, so you can't touch it.\n\nI'll make one more attempt: In landscape, try to scroll the Bestiary list by swiping on the visible filter chips area (which is above the list) — no, the list is below.\n\nOK, final: not re-reporting; mention in notes. Hmm, but \"Signing off while bugs remain is the worst outcome.\" If the landscape issue is real and I sign off, that's bad. But the developer explicitly couldn't reproduce it, so from the team's perspective it's not confirmed. I'll sign off with notes documenting it and my uncertainty. Alternatively, keep the session open? No, I should finish.\n\nWait, maybe I can find whether the app supports landscape by checking the Android manifest—can't read files/code. No.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the earlier successful portrait scrolling pattern: swipes only worked when I started on a *section header* (non-clickable) or blank areas; swipes starting on clickable rows often failed. In landscape, the only non-clickable areas near the list are the filter chips region (clickable) and the headers (the list is entirely below the fold). On the Home screen landscape, the visible Town header is clickable (\"Town\" collapsible). The blank area above (stats) is non-clickable, but I tried y=650 (between stats and Town) — that's within the scroll content? It might be a non-clickable stats row. It failed. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the app's scroll gesture requires dragging *up* starting in the scrollable container, but the container in landscape starts at y≈330 and its visible height is ~645. A drag from y=650 to y=200 (distance 450) should scroll. It didn't. So probably genuinely not scrollable.\n\nI think the app has a landscape layout bug. But the developer couldn't reproduce. The best I can do is file a second report with the Home screen (different from Gear) and clearer steps. L", "truncated": true}
