{"type": "thinking", "text": "The landscape Home screenshot shows:\n- Header, character, stats.\n- Town panel starting at y≈620 with only the tops of the cards visible (cards cut off at y=700 where the bottom nav begins).\n- Coins \"2.5M\" is cut off at the right edge by the system nav bar.\n- The rest of the Town grid, event, and session info are inaccessible.\n\nThis is definitely a landscape layout problem: content is cut off by the bottom nav and no scrolling. Note the app's content appears to be in a scrollable area starting around y=300, and the Town cards are cut at the nav. Can I scroll? I tried. But even if scrolling worked, the screenshot suggests the content extends below and the nav overlays it. If it were scrollable, you'd be able to scroll the Town panel up. Our swipe attempts failed. Also note the \"Town\" panel itself is collapsible; the cards row at the bottom cut off.\n\nHowever, this looks like the app's layout is simply too tall for landscape; the bottom nav is fixed at the bottom of the 1080 screen, and the content between the app bar (~215) and nav (~800) is only ~580px, while the Home content is designed for 2400px height. The app should scroll, but doesn't.\n\nGiven the severity (app barely usable in landscape), I think it's worth reporting despite the earlier rejection. I'll file it against the Home screen, describing the inability to reach Shop/Inn/Guild Hall (their cards are cut in half at the bottom nav), with the exact quote \"Town\" (visible) or the Coins cut-off. The element_ref: 8 (\"Town\" header) or 9/10/11 (unlabeled cards). The missing content is the issue; the quote \"Coins 2.5M\" is cut off at the right edge — that's a visible cut-off evidence. Actually the Coins value \"2.5M\" is partially cut by the system nav bar at the right edge (element 7 at 2274, but content width 2280?). Hmm.\n\nI'll file with element_ref 8 (Town header) and observed_quote \"Town\" — but that's not evidence of defect. Better: use the cut-off cards: element 9 at (442,856) [clickable] with no text — can't quote. The element 8 header is at y=779, and the cards at 856 are clipped.\n\nThe instructions allow omitting the quote for missing things. I'll omit observed_quote for this report, or use \"Town\" (it's on screen and marks the clipped section). I'll omit to be safe? \"a report about something missing may leave the quote out\" — yes, omit. But the report needs to describe observed. I'll mention the screenshot.\n\nLet me file: screen \"Home (landscape)\", element \"Town section / town destination cards\", symptom_type \"cut_off\", expected: content scrollable/fit so all town destinations, Gloomharvest and session status remain reachable in landscape. Observed: only top row cards partially visible, lower rows and event/session missing, no scroll.\n\nWait, but the earlier report for Gear said \"could not reproduce\". If this one is also rejected, fine. But maybe the developer will realize it's the same issue. I'll include a note that it's the same landscape clipping seen on other screens.\n\nHmm, should I risk it? The session's goal is to find bugs; unconfirmed reports are still reports. I'll file one more."}
