{"type": "thinking", "text": "No change, tools remain equipped. Fine.\n\nNow, I want to double-check the per-item trade-in bug is still reproducible after all these actions? It was confirmed, no need.\n\nFinal sign-off. But wait—should I check the \"Quest board\" change quickly? The instructions emphasize the listed areas. I'll skip.\n\nLet me consider if the \"Sell Old Gear\" preview total being correct is enough for the changed feature. Yes.\n\nOne more possible bug in the \"per-item trade-in\" changed feature: the reserved keeper quantity is computed \"from the inventory alone\" — maybe the bug manifests differently when the item is NOT equipped but quantity 1 and keeper ON: we saw a toast \"Keeping your last Bronze Dagger...\" — correct. And for Logs with keeper ON: 29 — correct. So only equipped double-count. Confirmed.\n\nNow let me draft the sign-off with notes: mention one confirmed bug (per-item), and note the two unconfirmed landscape reports (dev could not reproduce) so the team is aware.\n\nBefore sign-off, ensure the app is on a normal screen and no sheets open. Currently Profile → Gear. That's fine (no sheet). The keeper toggle is off, equipment restored, inventory Logs 30, gear per style restored (only Boots), search cleared? The Shop search was \"Stone\" but I left the shop; re-entry resets search. Fine. The \"Recent bulk sales\" record remains from the test bulk sale — expected.\n\nWait, the shop Sell tab's sort was left on \"Quantity\" (we tapped Quantity). Re-entering the shop might preserve the sort (it's not reset?). Earlier after leaving/re-entering, the sort showed Default. Let me check: after we set Quantity sort and left/re-entered? We left shop after that and re-entered multiple times; each time it showed Default checked. So sort resets. Fine.\n\nAlso the theme state: keeper OFF. Good.\n\nOne more thing: the \"Keep one of each item\" toggle state might be persisted across sessions; we set it off, matching precondition.\n\nAlso, we changed the per-item sell search etc. — no persistent effect.\n\nEquipment: all per-style armor slots empty; the weapons are only Iron Sword in Attack; the other styles have no weapon (as at start presumably). Boots in all styles? The Boots show in each style. If the boot was equipped in all styles by default, fine. If it was only in Attack and my actions copied it... no, I never equipped boots.\n\nLet me verify the Attack style quickly (Profile→View Combat Gear) to ensure the state matches the start: Weapon Iron Sword, Head/Body/Legs/Cape/Ring/Necklace/Shield None, Boots Bronze, DEF 75. We saw this earlier after restoring. After the Strength/Ranged/Magic restoration, Attack was untouched. Fine.\n\nSign off with confidence ~0.8 and notes.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the per-style loadout issue once more, because it could be a real bug that I dismissed: The inventory shows ONE Gilded Platebody. The \"Equip Best Gear\" button equipped it in all four combat styles simultaneously. Is that item duplication? If the game allows per-style loadouts, each loadout could reference the same item; when switching styles, the item is equipped. That's fine (like saved equipment presets). But the app also shows the Gilded Platebody as equipped in Strength, Ranged, Magic at the same time. If the game's equipment model allowed a single equipped item globally, then this is a bug. The existence of per-style tabs and style-specific weapon slots strongly indicates per-style loadouts are intended. So no report.\n\nBut wait, what about the stat display: each style shows different DEF based on its own loadout, which is consistent. Good.\n\nAlright, sign off.\n\nConfidence: I found and confirmed one bug; the listed areas otherwise look good. The landscape issue is unresolved/unconfirmed. Confidence 0.78.\n\nNotes: mention tested areas and the confirmed bug; mention landscape reports not reproduced by dev; mention data changes made (bulk junk sale, log sale/buy) for transparency? The sign-off notes can include that. Let's keep notes concise but informative.\n\nActually, should I mention the data changes? Yes, transparency: sold junk (Cowhide/Feather/Wool down to 1 each), sold/bought 1 Log (restored), no equipment left changed, keeper toggle off. That helps the next tester.\n\nSign off now."}
